WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.690
In Jerusalem, just after
Peter's sermon at Pentecost,

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.890
a new community of
believers begins to form.

3
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.500
Luke describes them meeting
daily in the Temple,

4
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.470
and breaking bread at home.

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.030
Then Luke adds something startling.

6
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.270
The believers sold their
possessions and goods.

7
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.180
Should churches today
still live like that?

8
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.940
In this mission, you'll
read the Acts 2 account,

9
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.600
and see what marked that first community.

10
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.960
Then you'll explore
what churches do today,

11
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:31.850
from worship to food banks,
and how traditions differ.

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:37.150
Your mission: weigh up how far the first
Christians are a model for churches today.
